# LCPC-2026-07-11 — canonical frozen counterexample dispositions.
#
# Standard P's counterexample rule requires the repository-owned reproducer to
# record, per mechanism, the EXPECTED FAILURE AGAINST THE FROZEN SUPERSEDED
# IMPLEMENTATION and the replacement pass. This file is that record. It is an
# INPUT to `simulateFrozenCounterexample`, not a restatement of its output:
# before Sprint 5.32 both halves were regenerated in-module from a composition
# constant, so the validation that checks them could not fail.
#
# Format: one row per CounterexampleMechanism, whitespace-separated.
#
#   <mechanism> <superseded-disposition> <replacement-disposition>
#
# Dispositions are `superseded-failure-observed` or
# `replacement-mechanism-closed`. Every mechanism in the compiled
# `CounterexampleMechanism` enumeration must appear exactly once; a missing,
# duplicated, or misspelled entry refuses the load rather than shrinking the
# counterexample's coverage silently.
#
# These rows participate in the frozen trace digest pinned by
# `frozenExpectedTraceDigest`, so an undeclared edit here refuses at load. The
# committed mutation fixture beside this file
# (`LCPC-2026-07-11.mutated.dispositions`) is the deliberate exception; see
# `FrozenTraceFixture` in
# `src/Prodbox/Test/Qualification/FrozenCounterexample.hs`.

AbsentGetAuthorityCasMismatch           superseded-failure-observed  replacement-mechanism-closed
GatewayDeadlineUnderThrottle            superseded-failure-observed  replacement-mechanism-closed
SelectedTargetAuthorityEndpointMismatch superseded-failure-observed  replacement-mechanism-closed
AppliedButResponseLostRetainedOperation superseded-failure-observed  replacement-mechanism-closed
FailedSiblingSkipsIndependentRestore    superseded-failure-observed  replacement-mechanism-closed
